  "summary": "Keys 1, 2 and 3 now select the glass, metal and fabric sphere. Typecheck passes and the render still looks as before. I did not press any keys in the headless render, so the spin itself is untested.\n\n- **Selection and spin:** the selected sphere spins about its vertical axis at 0.8 rad/s and the other two stay still. The number-row and numpad keys both work.\n- **State:** `window.__TASK_STATE__.selected` is `'glass' | 'metal' | 'fabric' | null`. It is `null` until a key is pressed.\n- **Why the files changed:** Aura3D can only set a bridged node's transform at load time, so I could not spin a sphere inside the single combined model. `recipes/studio.mjs` now takes a `part` param. I imported it four times: the cyclorama under the existing `studio` name, plus `glass`, `metal` and `fabric`. `src/three-bridge/studio.scene.ts` places each sphere model at its row position with its own runtime id, and `src/main.ts` sets position and rotation each frame.\n- **Spin visibility:** spin is only clearly visible on the fabric sphere, because its weave is asymmetric. I added faint column variation to the metal's brushed texture, but the glass and metal highlights stay put under fixed lights, so their spin is subtle."
